---
title: Ardeidae
---
# Ardeidae

Ardeidae is the heron, egret and bittern family, long-legged wading birds that
catch fish from above the water. A heron hunts by standing still in the
shallows and striking downward as a fish comes within reach; it does not enter
the water, and it cannot follow a fish that goes deep. The neck folds into an S
at rest and straightens explosively in the strike, powered by a kinked sixth
vertebra unique to the family. See [[grey-heron]].
